WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.718
Automatic dialing places calls for your agents, so it needs guardrails.

00:00:05.718 --> 00:00:11.601
This video covers the abandoned-call settings of a dialer profile, Predictive pacing, what

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:15.400
the dialer does with every record, and how retries work.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.841
With Power, Progressive and Predictive dialing, the customer is dialed first.

00:00:25.841 --> 00:00:29.360
An agent is connected once a person answers.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:34.573
A call is abandoned when a person answers and no agent is connected

00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:36.590
to them within two seconds.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.280
The person hears silence, or hangs up.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.784
Rules in many places limit how many calls may be abandoned.

00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:48.059
A dialer profile measures the rate, can stop dialing at a limit, and

00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:49.503
can play a message.

00:00:49.503 --> 00:00:51.756
Confirm which rules apply to you:

00:00:51.756 --> 00:00:55.510
the settings do not make a campaign compliant on their own.

00:00:59.785 --> 00:01:03.171
Open the profile, and find the Abandoned calls card.

00:01:03.171 --> 00:01:07.842
Measured abandonment at the top shows the rate over the rolling window and

00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:11.054
over the last 30 days, with the counts behind it.

00:01:11.054 --> 00:01:14.615
It is zero here, because this site has placed no calls.

00:01:15.263 --> 00:01:21.133
Tick Enforce an abandonment-rate cap, and automated dialing pauses while too many answered

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.723
calls find no agent.

00:01:23.197 --> 00:01:28.250
Maximum abandonment rate is the cap, as a share of the calls a person answered.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:33.303
Abandonment sample floor is how many answered calls the window needs before the

00:01:33.303 --> 00:01:37.167
cap applies, so a few early calls cannot stop the campaign.

00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:41.916
Play a message when a call is abandoned plays your message instead of

00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:43.503
hanging up in silence.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:47.075
A warning shows while it is off, and the cap needs it on.

00:01:47.543 --> 00:01:50.434
Abandoned call message is what the person hears.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:53.752
Say who is calling, and give a number to call back or to

00:01:53.752 --> 00:01:55.518
ask not to be called again.

00:01:55.518 --> 00:01:59.372
The site name and the number the person was called from are filled

00:01:59.372 --> 00:02:00.603
in for each call.

00:02:02.203 --> 00:02:05.885
Measured abandonment counts only calls a person answered.

00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:10.502
It is measured for each profile, not for each campaign, so campaigns that

00:02:10.502 --> 00:02:13.073
share a profile are measured together.

00:02:17.257 --> 00:02:21.118
Choose Predictive, and the Predictive pacing card appears.

00:02:21.118 --> 00:02:24.437
Pacing is One call per reserved agent by default.

00:02:24.437 --> 00:02:29.203
Each call reserves its own available agent, and fewer calls are placed as

00:02:29.203 --> 00:02:31.677
the abandonment rate nears the cap.

00:02:32.131 --> 00:02:37.829
Over-dial places more calls than there are free agents, because most calls are not answered.

00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:42.247
The Target abandonment rate is what it steers toward, and it must stay

00:02:42.247 --> 00:02:44.631
below the Maximum abandonment rate.

00:02:45.369 --> 00:02:49.524
Lines per agent is the most calls ringing for each free agent.

00:02:49.524 --> 00:02:53.984
Calls in flight is the most calls ringing at once for one campaign.

00:02:53.984 --> 00:02:57.589
Both stay in force whatever the answer rate suggests.

00:02:58.047 --> 00:03:00.747
The answer rate must be trusted first.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:05.410
Answer rate sample floor is how many calls need an outcome, and Answer

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.539
rate window is how far back they are counted.

00:03:08.539 --> 00:03:12.467
Until then, the profile dials one call per reserved agent.

00:03:12.922 --> 00:03:17.396
Count agents about to free up adds agents expected to finish soon.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:21.248
Connect wait is how long a person may wait for an agent.

00:03:21.248 --> 00:03:27.152
Zero is recommended, because a call not connected within two seconds counts as abandoned.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:32.310
Retry abandoned calls only with an agent reserved is on by default, so

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.223
no one is abandoned twice.

00:03:34.223 --> 00:03:38.587
Over-dial needs the cap, the message and a target below the cap, so

00:03:38.587 --> 00:03:41.397
the profile cannot be saved without them.

00:03:41.856 --> 00:03:45.660
Turn on the cap and the message, and the profile saves.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.776
The list now shows a Power profile and a Predictive profile.

00:03:51.376 --> 00:03:55.239
With over-dial, no agent is reserved while calls ring.

00:03:55.239 --> 00:04:00.389
When a person answers, the free agent who has waited longest is connected.

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:06.956
If nobody is free, the person hears the abandoned-call message and the call counts as abandoned.

00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:11.478
Over-dial does not start until it can trust its numbers.

00:04:11.478 --> 00:04:15.433
Until then, and whenever the rate is at or near the cap, it

00:04:15.433 --> 00:04:17.866
dials one call per reserved agent.

00:04:17.866 --> 00:04:21.456
It stops altogether when the rate cannot be measured.

00:04:25.656 --> 00:04:28.650
Before every call, the dialer checks in order:

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:32.797
the number is valid and not out of service, attempts are left, the

00:04:32.797 --> 00:04:37.346
retry delay has passed, the contact has not opted out, the calling window

00:04:37.346 --> 00:04:42.356
is open, the cap allows dialing, and the number is not on a do-not-call registry.

00:04:43.106 --> 00:04:46.217
A record with no valid number becomes Failed.

00:04:46.217 --> 00:04:49.267
A record with no attempts left is Completed.

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:53.293
A record on a do-not-call list, or with a number known to be

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:56.954
out of service, becomes Cancelled and is never dialed.

00:04:56.954 --> 00:05:00.126
Anything else is tried again in a later cycle.

00:05:00.876 --> 00:05:07.065
A call that ends before an agent is connected is dispositioned by the dialer itself:

00:05:07.065 --> 00:05:14.217
No answer, Busy, Answering machine, Rejected, Call failed, Disconnected, or Number not in service.

00:05:14.217 --> 00:05:17.656
The agent never sees it, and has no wrap-up.

00:05:21.856 --> 00:05:24.197
The subject flow decides first.

00:05:24.197 --> 00:05:28.815
If its Try Again action sets Maximum attempts, that number is used.

00:05:28.815 --> 00:05:32.864
If it leaves it empty, the profile's Max attempts is used.

00:05:32.864 --> 00:05:36.976
If the flow has a disposition for how the call ended but no

00:05:36.976 --> 00:05:40.076
Try Again, the contact is not called again.

00:05:40.826 --> 00:05:44.891
If the flow has no disposition for how the call ended, the dialer

00:05:44.891 --> 00:05:49.930
dispositions the call with the matching outcome, and calls the contact again after

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:53.136
the Retry delay, up to the profile's Max attempts.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:58.752
A date picked when the call is dispositioned, or the Try Again action's

00:05:58.752 --> 00:06:02.037
Default schedule hours, sets the next attempt.

00:06:02.037 --> 00:06:06.145
Otherwise it is dialed after the Retry delay, never sooner.

00:06:06.145 --> 00:06:11.516
Only calls that rang out, were busy, reached a machine, or dropped are retried.

00:06:11.516 --> 00:06:17.456
Attempts count across follow-ups, so a limit of three means the first call and two more.

00:06:21.656 --> 00:06:25.381
A long list and a small team uses Power with one or two

00:06:25.381 --> 00:06:29.716
calls per agent, so agents spend their time talking, not dialing.

00:06:30.466 --> 00:06:34.527
A campaign under calling rules turns on the cap and the message, and

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:37.546
reads Measured abandonment during the first days.

00:06:38.296 --> 00:06:43.596
Numbers that were not answered are called again on their own, within the limits you set.

00:06:45.596 --> 00:06:49.987
Choose how calls are paced, protect the people who answer, and let the

00:06:49.987 --> 00:06:53.454
subject flow and the profile decide what happens next.

00:06:53.454 --> 00:06:54.956
Thanks for watching.

